      "quoted_tweet_id": null,
      "retweeted_tweet_id": null,
      "text": "Thank you to everyone who has expressed concern for the wellbeing of our U.S. Coast Guard responders as they continue to work closely with our partners following the aircraft collision over the Potomac.\n\nWe could not complete our mission to bring closure for the families affected by this tragedy without your support.\n\nThe Coast Guard is dedicated to ensuring our members have 24/7 access to both Coast Guard Chaplains as well as our Critical Incident Stress Management (CISM) team members who are trained to provide Psychological First Aid during major incidents.\n\nThank you again and #SemperParatus\n\n@uscgmidatlantic @uscglantarea #coastguard",
      "text_resolved": "Thank you to everyone who has expressed concern for the wellbeing of our U.S. Coast Guard responders as they continue to work closely with our partners following the aircraft collision over the Potomac.\n\nWe could not complete our mission to bring closure for the families affected by this tragedy without your support.\n\nThe Coast Guard is dedicated to ensuring our members have 24/7 access to both Coast Guard Chaplains as well as our Critical Incident Stress Management (CISM) team members who are trained to provide Psychological First Aid during major incidents.\n\nThank you again and #SemperParatus\n\n@uscgmidatlantic @uscglantarea #coastguard",
